<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      macOS bundle entitlements for Flowix.

      用于 `tauri.conf.production.json` 的 `bundle.macOS.entitlements` 字段;
      由 codesign 使用 runtime options 和本 entitlements 文件完成签名。
      见 `scripts/sign-cli.sh`。

      v4 rationale:
      - allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory ── rllm crate 跟部分 Rust
        动态库需要运行时生成可执行内存, Apple notarization 允许这两条
        entitlement 配合 hardened runtime。
      - disable-library-validation ── 允许加载未 Apple 签名的 .dylib
        (rllm / 第三方 Rust 依赖)。
      - network.client ── IPC 跟 AI provider 走 https。
      - network.server ── tauri://localhost webview 跟 IPC bridge。
    -->

    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
      Native Sign in with Apple via AuthenticationServices.

      DISABLED for v1.1.6 packaging: Apple Developer Portal profile
      generation for App ID `com.flowix.app` (Team `9FJ9ZD86C2`) is
      returning a cached .provisionprofile whose Entitlements dictionary
      does not include `com.apple.developer.applesignin`, even though
      the App ID has the capability enabled in the Portal UI and the
      Profile UI lists "Sign In with Apple" as an Enabled Capability.
      Delete + regenerate returns the identical cached payload (same
      ExpirationDate, same file size), confirming an Apple backend
      stale-state issue.

      With hardened runtime + the binary claiming this Apple-only
      entitlement, amfid rejects at launch with `Failure validating
      against provisioning profiles` (amfid log), surfacing to the
      user as `RBSRequestErrorDomain Code=5 / NSPOSIXErrorDomain
      Code=163 "Launchd job spawn failed"`.

      TODO before re-enabling: contact Apple Developer Support to
      force-push the Sign in with Apple capability registration, then
      regenerate the provisioning profile and verify the Entitlements
      dictionary contains `com.apple.developer.applesignin`. Uncomment
      the block below once verified.
    -->
    <!--
    <key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
    <array>
        <string>Default</string>
    </array>
    -->

    <!--
      User-selected directories are persisted with security-scoped bookmarks
      in `security_bookmark.rs`. These entitlements are required for the
      standard macOS sandbox/bookmark model and are harmless for local
      ad-hoc/dev builds that do not enable the app sandbox.

      Do not enable `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` here yet: Flowix runs
      local agents / CLI tools, and a full sandbox would need a broader
      audit of child process and workspace access.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.files.bookmarks.app-scope</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
